{#- Price as a confounder: reported either way — a weak correlation means price
    cannot explain the ranking on its own, not that price is irrelevant. -#}
{% if category_price_rho is not none -%}
<p class="caveat-note"><strong>Price is not controlled.</strong> Across ranked product-type pages, the median price of the products they list and their seen → carted rate have a rank correlation of {{ category_price_rho|fmt('+.2f') }} ({{ category_price_p|pval }}). {% if category_price_p >= 0.05 %}That is too weak to explain the ranking on its own, but cheaper items may still be an easier yes (see the price bands below), so a low rate is not proof of a presentation problem.{% else %}Pages listing cheaper products convert better, so part of each gap may be price, not presentation.{% endif %}</p>
{%- endif %}
